A||||2||Alex2004||adding dome light supervision w/ keyless entry question(s)||||5||
Z||000000||Alex2004||06-18-2001||01:40 PM||||I installed keyless entry on my fiero and it has the option for dome light supervision and so i ordered the relay for that also, i am having trouble getting it to work, i even called bulldog security but i'm still doing something wrong w/ the wiring. the manual just shows how to wire the relay to which wires but i cannot seem to find the dome light circut wire.  Here is what the manual says, there are 5 wires and they are numbered. <BR>#87 to dome light circut, <BR>#85 12 V constant<BR>#30 (+) or (-) depending on door type, If (+) Fuse at 20 amps, <BR>#86 (-) violet from module & one of the wire on the relay isn't used, now here is the way i connected it.<BR>#87 white wire at the door pin switch<BR>#85 connect to 12v cst. at the fuse box<BR>#30 (this is the one i'm confused on) the tan wire on the door pin<BR>#86 is connected to the module.  So can someone tell me what i'm doing wrong? before it just kept blowing the fuse but now i did something and it's not blowing the fuse now, but it's still not making the dome light come on... Let me know if you can figure it out.<BR>Thanks, Alex...    <A HREF="mailto:Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A>   <BR>PS i have wired #87 to the dome light wire also (orange one) and it still was blowing the fuse.<BR>Oh, its a bulldog keyless entry system, model #1402<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||06-18-2001||02:30 PM||||Alright. The Fiero domelights are tripped by a NEGATIVE wire. This means the orange wire is ALWAYS hot with power. Then, when the door is opened, the switch in the door jamb closes, and makes the white wire a ground.<P>So, the coil on the relay consists of terminals(wires) #85 and #86. The common terminal is #30, Normally closed is #87a, and normally open is #87.<P>You said that #85 should be hooked to constant power, so therefor the brain of your system has to make #86 a ground in order to turn the lights on.<P>#87 is connected correctly<BR>#85 is connected correctly<BR>#30 is connected incorrectly, this is your problem: #30 is the common terminal, so in the case of the Fiero, (since tripped by ground) you want to connect #30 to a constant ground, not the tan door pin wire. Connect this to a constant ground, or make your own to a screw or somthing (if you do, make sure it works as a good grounding point)<P>#86 is connected corretly<P>You need to change the #30 to a constant ground, and there is no reason this wire needs to be fused, beacuse the Fiero ssystem is tripped by a ground wire. LMK how this works out!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||06-18-2001||03:34 PM||||THANKS SEANH!!!! YOU RULE.... It works now...<BR>Thanks so much b/c it was really pissing me off why it wasn't working...LOL...thanks again!<P>Alex...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
